  {
   "id": "b3",
   "function": "explanation",
   "scene_type": "zlx_cutaway",
   "spoken": "The octane number describes knock resistance, as Chevron's fuel review puts it. In other words, how well the petrol resists self-ignition before the flame from the spark arrives. It is measured in a test engine against isooctane, rated one hundred, and normal heptane, rated zero.",
   "data": {
    "title": "Knock resistance",
    "knock": true,
    "notes": [
