   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "b4",
   "function": "demonstration",
   "scene_type": "zlx_cutaway",
   "spoken": "So higher octane helps where knock is holding the engine back. According to the engineering lecture, a knock sensor then pulls the spark timing back, and the engine no longer fires at the best moment. The lecture lists many measures against knock: cooling, charge air cooling, fast combustion, and higher octane.",
   "data": {
    "title": "At the knock limit",
    "knock": true,
